// arithmetic operators to decide when to explicitly open a visible "<< >>"
// computation span. Inside spans, the parser is the hard authority: the
// strategy uses adaptive/group-aware constrained decoding, with a mild
// repetition penalty and caller-supplied token-group preferences, and closes
// the span as soon as the constrained prefix is complete. This state supports
// the task by separating free natural-language reasoning from parser-checked
// arithmetic snippets that must appear between visible delimiters.
